      "message": "Although it\u0027s possible to \"mock\" the file system to behave case-sensitive/-insensitive for this test case, testing this against the real file system behavior should be preferred in my opinion.\n\nOther tests achieve this by using `org.junit.Assume` (see for example `org.eclipse.jgit.util.HookTest` or `org.eclipse.jgit.indexdiff.IndexDiffWithSymlinkTest`). `FS` already provides the case-sensitivity information via `org.eclipse.jgit.util.FS.isCaseSensitive()`.\n\nThat said: As far as I can tell, all tests are only run on a linux test runner, so some of these test cases would not run in CI at all (but this is already an existing problem, e.g. for `org.eclipse.egit.core.internal.util.RepositoryPathCheckerTest.testLocalAbsoluteFileWindows()`)",
